From 826c3fbb4cd05249d6a322925a6ce171a67de74e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:21:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/51] Move the cached subtitles browser to a second-level
 page with thumbnails and export

The cache browser used to be a plain two-line list inside a dialog.
It is now a proper settings sub-page reached through the standard
android:fragment navigation, and each entry shows the video still
resolved from the recorded video id, the video title and the
translation details.

- BisubCacheFragment: RecyclerView list that reloads on resume, an
  empty-state message, and the viewer dialog moved over from the
  settings fragment
- tapping an entry opens the full text; the viewer now offers
  exporting the .vtt anywhere on the device through the system
  save-as dialog (ACTION_CREATE_DOCUMENT) next to deleting it
- thumbnails load through PicassoHelper from the YouTube still of
  the video id; unknown ids keep the placeholder image
- the old dialog-based list, viewer and delete flow are removed
  from BisubSettingsFragment along with their now-unused imports
